From 3864f5033b37f4701618808f5ed6ba5061f8365b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:01:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Free TV's Xumo streams get a guide from Xumo's own JSON
 schedule
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Xumo publishes no XMLTV file, so its ~29 streams stayed blank while every
other installed source had a feed. The platform does expose a JSON schedule,
and this translates it to XMLTV in memory for the existing importer - no
second importer, no second swap, no new matcher pass, so prune, the staged
swap, the empty-feed guard and the profile pin are all the ones already
tested.

Live verification corrected three things the community generator implies:
the channel list is a separate endpoint (the schedule response carries ids
with no titles), the URL's trailing number is a six-hour block rather than a
day page, and the API's `+0000` offset is not a spelling the guide parser
accepts - the first run emitted 455 channels and zero programmes because of
it, which is why the adapter has its own timestamp parser.

The adapter is an installed source, not a line in the Extra EPG field: it
registers by per-profile flag, reads LAST so no existing source's precedence
moves, and is imported alone rather than re-downloading the other six.

