From 5c20f3d2d44afbdfb6b17e5cfe046550f4047e2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:11:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Two fatal crashes: a refused player launch and a
 duplicated list key
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Both were caught by Sentry on real devices and both are fatal, so neither can
wait for a redesign.

ANDROID-12 (0.9.67): the stream screen launches the player from a
LaunchedEffect, and when ActivityTaskManager refuses that launch the
platform throws a bare `RuntimeException: Failure from system` out of
composition - the app died instead of telling the viewer the player would
not open. The launch is now reported, not propagated.

ANDROID-11: the calendar used the watched-state key as its LazyColumn key,
but a day can legitimately hold the same show/season/episode twice, and
Compose rejects the duplicate key with a fatal IllegalArgumentException.
Row identity is now the watched key plus its occurrence, so the first row
keeps the key watched state is stored under.

